.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_rules" "fuzzygene_rules"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_rules \- Export the IF-THEN rules of every fitted target gene.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_rules(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Export the IF-THEN rules of every fitted target gene.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a character vector, one element per rule (with per gene section headers)
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Each line reads like
 `rule3 [12.34%] IF TF-A IS high AND TF-B IS low THEN gene-G = 1.2*TF-A + -0.8*TF-B + 0.1`：
 the bracketed number is the average normalized firing strength on the training set, the
 coefficients are the local linear conclusions of that rule.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
